Q: Get the middle two items of an array with even number of items A: <p>My favorite is this approach:</p>
<pre><code>function middleItems(arr) {
  return [arr[Math.floor((arr.length - 1) / 2)], arr[Math.floor(arr.length / 2)]];
}
</code></pre>
<p>This returns two elements in the middle for even sized arrays and for odd sized arrrays returns the middle element twice.</p>

Q: Signal doesn&#39;t update when creating a new array of objects A: <p>The track property must be a unique property among the elements in the array.</p>
<p>Maybe the files have the same name, which is messing up the <code>@for</code>, try tracking by <code>$index</code> instead.</p>
<pre><code>        @for (file of uploadedFiles(); track $index; let i = $index) {
            &lt;div class=&quot;gallery-item&quot;&gt;
                &lt;img [src]=&quot;file.data&quot; alt=&quot;{{ file.name }}&quot; class=&quot;gallery-image&quot;&gt;
                &lt;div class=&quot;file-name&quot;&gt;{{ file.name }}&lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;button mat-icon-button type=&quot;button&quot; (click)=&quot;setPrimary(i)&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;mat-icon&gt;{{ file.isPrimary ? 'star' : 'star_border' }}&lt;/mat-icon&gt;
                &lt;/button&gt;
                &lt;button mat-icon-button type=&quot;button&quot; (click)=&quot;removeFile(i)&quot; class=&quot;delete-btn&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;mat-icon&gt;close&lt;/mat-icon&gt;
                &lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;/div&gt;
        }
</code></pre>
<p>The <code>set</code> and <code>update</code> do the same thing, the later provides the state inside the callback, which is for convenience (As per my understanding).</p>
